<title>UK: LASMO to enter power generating - newspaper.</title>
<headline>LASMO to enter power generating - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exploration and production company LASMO Plc is planning to diversify into power generating in a bid to develop end uses for some of its gas reserves, the Sunday Telegraph reported.</p>
<p>The board has agreed the move in principle and is looking into power stations in Indonesia and Pakistan, the paper said.</p>
<p>The Telegraph said LASMO wanted to take minority stakes of about 20 percent in gas-fired power stations in alliances with power companies and engineering groups.</p>
<p>No one at the company was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717))</p>
